WEBVTT

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:03.690
The morning comes early for the Yorishiro craftsman.
[*Yorishiro is the object representative of a divine spirit]

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.770
At first, Yorishiro only worked for a short time,

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.570
but once she got the trick
of kneading magic power into it,

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.610
its lifespan gradually lengthened.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.370
Kneading...

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:19.080
- Clothes are sewn by hand.
- Sewing...

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.540
She doesn't mind detailed work,

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:22.960
so she makes them patiently.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.000
She's happy
when she can make something cute.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.300
I can hardly move the joints.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.680
I want to look cooler!

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.640
I want a taller figure with a raised head!

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.430
I want my clothes to be high-leg!

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:42.350
Yes.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:46.060
She responds to her client's
unreasonable requests with sincerity.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:48.610
Shapeen! Momo,

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:50.730
thank you so much
for the beautiful Yorishiro!

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.490
My mouth is saying thank you on its own.

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:54.400
No! This is not how I really feel.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.450
Thank you!

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:56.160
Stop it!

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.370
It's messing with my ego!

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.990
Shapeen! Thank you!

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:02.660
Good Yorishiro can be also
remotely controlled.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.130
Shamiko is sleepy after
all that happened at her part-time job.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:13.920
No, no, no.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.430
Oh, Shamiko.

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:18.590
I'm not sick, so
you don't have to look after me.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:19.430
Nope.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.980
Are you giving her something
in return for her work?

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:26.730
Shamiko, is there something you want?

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:27.940
Why do you ask this?

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.520
Give me a Yorishiro ticket!

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.190
Just say whatever you want.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:34.240
- Then, an ice cream cone.
- Give me a Yorishiro ticket!

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.400
Not that kind of thing
that disappears after you eat it.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.950
You said whatever I want!

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:59.050
(The Demon Girl Next Door Season 2)

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:12.960
(Beat it!
Operation to Retrieve the Peach Shamiko!)

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.010
According to the address on her resume,
she's supposed to be here.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.050
Master, you're looking suspicious!

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.850
You are...

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.010
The magical girl?! Why are you here?

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.350
Because I live here.

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:32.150
It didn't say on her resume
that she had a bodyguard!

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:33.560
Let's run away, Rico!

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.070
I don't like the word "run away".

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:37.780
Then turn around and go forward!

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.780
Hey, please calm down.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:40.900
Keep going!

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:41.950
Ah!

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:42.740
What?

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.080
Apology?

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.660
I know I bothered you the other day, Yuko.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:56.040
I heard you had some questions for me,
so I thought I'd come out to see you.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.250
Aren't there any more injuries?

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:02.090
Never mind, I just
flew away lightly in the hallway.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.380
I'm sorry,

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:05.850
I'm new to an animal client.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:07.970
I hope you will like this.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.560
Oh, is that your mother?

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.270
I'm an omnivore, so don't mind me.

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.520
We'll just have some sushi pockets.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:14.730
Without vinegar.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.270
Rico, please don't do that.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:19.150
Ms. Sakura is missing? I see...

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:24.240
I have searched for her by various means
since I came back to town,

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.200
but all have failed.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:29.910
Perhaps my sister is now in a state of cores.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:33.620
Momo, can I listen to the talks about Sakura?

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:34.370
Ryo...

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:37.170
I said I would help your sister,

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:40.460
and my research is about
the house and the town,

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.010
so I think it would be useful.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.470
Yes, please.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:46.550
(About the search for Ms. Sakura)
Great! I'll be doing summarizing beside you!

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.180
(About the search for Ms. Sakura)
It can be a little simpler.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:52.480
I've only met Ms. Sakura a few times.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:56.150
The last time I saw her was
on Christmas Day ten years ago.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.940
Ten years ago...

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.030
It was right
before the coffee shop opened,

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:02.650
so I'm pretty sure that's the time.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:06.070
At that time,
I had just arrived in this town

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:09.030
and was preparing to
work thanks to Ms. Sakura's help.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:11.370
While I was preparing for the opening,

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:14.080
Ms. Sakura popped in.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:19.790
Hey there. The ward at
the entrance has been upgraded!

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:23.260
Thank you, Ms. Sakura,
for everything you have done for us.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:26.050
Oh, something like
a natural disaster is coming now,

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.970
so lock up for a couple of days!

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:29.220
And don't go out!

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.970
And hire this girl!

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:33.600
She wants to cook!

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:34.850
Looking forward to working with you!

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:37.060
Who is this girl?
What's the natural disaster?

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:39.360
Sorry, I'm in a hurry, another time!

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:45.280
That's when I was made to hire Rico.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:49.150
This is the last time we saw Ms. Sakura.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:52.830
She didn't come to eat our food.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:54.500
She promised.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.580
Sakura, I wonder where she is.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:01.330
The core moves and runs away,
so it's hard to find it.

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:02.380
Oh, it moves?

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:04.630
Have you seen the core?

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:08.260
Where I'm from, it's called a spirit.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:08.340
I saw one before I came to this town.

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:11.180
(Cha cha) (Spirit)
I saw one before I came to this town.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.060
The cores I saw

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.750
(Remember!)
were a little monkey and a butterfly.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.270
Both of them were carried away

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:19.020
by a priestess who was one of our allies.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:21.400
Rico, what were you doing
before you came here?

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.650
The core I saw before

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:26.190
was in crystal form and did not move.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.860
So it has an animal form, too?

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:30.620
Let me talk a little too.

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:33.700
Momo was looking for the core
as something that doesn't move.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.660
According to the information
from the fox there,

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.580
cores can be an animal form
that moves and runs away.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:39.790
If we ask around differently,

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:42.040
we might get some new information.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:45.000
That's all we know.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.840
If there's anything else,
please let us help.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.630
Yuko's not getting enough sleep,

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:51.300
so I think it's time to call it a night, Rico.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.300
Which button do I press to play this?

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:56.600
You press the red button and
then choose a name for your character.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:56.970
(Adventure book 1/2/3)

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:57.520
(Adventure book 1/2/3)
Oh.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:58.140
(Adventure book 1/2/3)

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.310
(Adventure book 1/2/3)
Which adventure book is the best one?

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:01.730
(Adventure book 1/2/3)
Let's see... Number 2...

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:03.150
(Adventure book 1/2/3)
Rico, be careful!

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:05.110
(Adventure book 2 is deleted)

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:07.150
(Adventure book 2 is deleted)
I told you to be careful.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:12.280
If you don't mind, would you
be willing to work for us again?

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:13.660
Yes, with pleasure.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:14.330
Eh?

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:16.910
Perhaps I can find some good clues

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:18.290
if I get to know more people.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.250
Thank you, Yuko,

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:24.170
but sometimes I feel
that someone is strongly against it.

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:25.710
Never mind!

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.800
Momo and I are fighting together,

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.170
but we're enemies actually.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:31.550
Maybe she doesn't want me
to take the initiative

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:34.550
because I've been coming up
with all kinds of clues lately!

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:35.810
No!

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:39.020
Why do you come up with
twisted interpretations all the time?

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.020
No part-time job, no working, no way!

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:41.600
Huh?

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:44.860
I'm sorry, I want to find my sister,

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:48.650
but I don't want Shamiko to get involved
in any more weird stuff, perhaps.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.900
Why? Something's wrong with Momo today!

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.530
For now,

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:54.910
please consider it.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:56.910
This is a gift for you.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.040
Thank you!

00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:58.120
(Tamasakura sweet bun)

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:59.830
(Tamasakura sweet bun)
It's Tamasakura!

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:00.710
(Tamasakura sweet bun)
You know it?

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:02.670
Momo loves it.

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:03.420
Right, Momo?

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:04.750
I don't like it!

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:07.130
It just so bothers me that
it interferes with my life!

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:09.090
Well, you seem to like it a lot!

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:12.340
Actually, I designed Tamasakura!

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:14.590
You're the creator of Tamasakura?

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:18.140
I can't believe it has fans here!
I'm so happy!

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:21.230
Momo! I want to get along with you too!

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:23.770
And I want to put in
a lot of shifts for Yuko!

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:26.810
Next time we meet, I'll give you
lots of limited-edition goods!

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:27.900
No, thank you!

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.280
T-shirts! Fans!

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:30.360
No, thank you!

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:31.860
Phone cards!

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:34.240
Who needs a phone card nowadays?
No, thanks!

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:36.070
Phone card with autograph!

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:39.950
Phone card with autograph
and a Polaroid ticket!

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:41.540
Thank you...

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:42.460
Momo gave in.

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:43.000
(Tamasakura embedded in meat)

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.600
(Tamasakura embedded in meat)
This is the Tamasakura that Momo gave me!

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:49.090
But why do you like Tamasakura so much?

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:50.420
It's because...

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:56.050
Because it looks like my sister.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:57.430
It looks like Sakura?

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:03.270
(Come here, come here)
Come here, come here, come here...

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.190
(I have sweets!)
I have sweets!

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:07.770
I can't picture Chiyoda Sakura anymore.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:08.770
(Did it look like her?)
Did it look like her?

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:10.520
It's not that they have similar faces!

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.400
It's the parts
and the coloring that are similar!

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:13.820
Like when she transformed!

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.650
What?

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:17.620
Could it be that my sister was the model?

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:18.910
No, no.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:22.950
I have never seen Sakura
in her transformed form.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:26.710
The model for Tamasakura
is the fairy I saw.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.630
The day the cafe opened,

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:31.960
(Year-end big sale)
I went shopping at night.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:34.050
(Year-end big sale)
To the shopping center Maruma.

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:36.090
And then,

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:39.350
a mysterious cat ran.

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:41.810
She wore an unusual red-and-white collar.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.850
It was snowing, but there were no footprints,

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.980
and petals were scattered
on the path we walked.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.730
The cat looked at me, bowed,

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:02.120
and disappeared as if melting into
the wall of the building next door.

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:05.250
After that, my shop thrived!

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:09.630
I think of that cat as a fairy who
makes everyone happy who sees her!

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:15.380
That's why used its appearance
as a motif for the application...

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:16.590
Mr. Taipiridae, one more time!

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:18.340
What you just said, one more time!

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:20.890
Stop squeezing the customer's nose, Ryo!

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:24.140
But what he's talking about
is very important!

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:27.100
What day and what month
was it when you saw the cat?

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.100
Stop it!

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:30.600
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:32.150
Let me see...

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:36.490
The anniversary of our opening
was 10 years ago, on December 28th.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:37.320
I'll summarize it!

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:40.740
According to Mr. Taipiridae,

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.370
the last time he saw Sakura
was December 25.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.990
Only three days passed
before we saw the cat, right?

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:46.910
According to Miss Fox,

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.660
cores move in the form of animals.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.630
Besides, normal cats don't melt into walls

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.500
and they don't produce petals.

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:54.960
So I think,

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:58.420
that cat might be Sakura's core.

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:03.510
Maybe we should look for the cat
with a red and white collar.

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:05.890
This is Ryo's free research,

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:06.890
a map of the town.

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.940
Where did the cat go and
where did it disappear into the wall?

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:15.480
Uh, through the fountain square
in front of the shopping center Maruma,

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:17.480
the building across the street.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:19.990
The building across from Maruma is...

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.910
Seiki Memorial Hospital.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:25.990
Oh, this is the hospital where
I was hospitalized when I was little.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:27.700
Oh, Shamiko,

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.540
do you remember seeing cats 10 years ago?

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:32.250
I'm sorry, I don't remember at all!

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:34.380
It was a long time ago after all.

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:37.050
Anyway, let's call Seiki Memorial Hospital.

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:39.010
Yuko must have seen the cat!

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:39.670
Eh?

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:44.260
I remember Yuko talking about
the cat at the hospital.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:45.640
Tea for your mother!

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:46.890
I'll serve you a cushion too!

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:49.060
Do you want to eat sushi pocket with us?

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:51.690
I'm the host in this house, so don't mind me.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:52.350
(Inari sushi [sushi pocket])

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:54.860
(Inari sushi [sushi pocket])
Sushi rice wrapped in fried bean curd

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:57.480
(Inari sushi [sushi pocket])
seasoned with soy sauce, sugar, mirin, etc.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:58.510
(Inari sushi [sushi pocket])
There are many variations,

00:11:58.510 --> 00:11:59.820
(Inari sushi [sushi pocket])
with or without ingredients inside,

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:03.450
(Inari sushi [sushi pocket])
with strong or weak flavors,

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:04.950
(Inari sushi [sushi pocket])
but they are all delicious!

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:08.370
At that time, Yuko was doing her best
in medical treatment.

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:09.080
(Ten years ago, Seki Memorial Hospital)

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:12.160
(Ten years ago, Seki Memorial Hospital)
One day, Yuko woke up and said to me.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:16.250
Mom, a white cat came to my room.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:18.710
I talked with the cat.

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.300
But it disappeared.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:24.550
At the time,
Yuko had respiratory problems,

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:27.220
so we searched all over
the hospital with the nurses

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.720
for any stray cats that
might have gotten into the hospital.

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:33.730
But we couldn't find
any trace of the cat anywhere.

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:36.650
It might have been Yuko's dream.

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:38.650
It's impossible for an animal to talk.

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:40.150
Master, that's not good.

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:41.280
Look in the mirror.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:44.070
It's the final month of pregnancy,

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:45.740
so it's the end of the year 10 years ago.

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:48.160
Right after Mr. Taipiridae saw the cat.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.870
Unless that wasn't Shamiko's dream.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:55.790
10 years ago,
Shamiko contacted Sakura's Core.

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:59.920
And it's possible
they were talking about something.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:03.010
Shamiko! Do you remember
having a talk with the cat?

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.800
I don't remember
such an interesting experience!

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:08.050
Try to remember!
Try to remember! Twist it!

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:08.220
Stop using my horns as handles!

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.470
(Stop using my horns as handles!)
Stop using my horns as handles!

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:13.520
Oh, Momo is back to her normal self!
Calm down!

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.190
That's not the point!

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:17.310
I'm not twisting the two handles,
so think of that!

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:19.360
- Come on, Shamiko!
- If I think I have to remember,

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:20.520
- Remember what's important!
- I can't come up with anything else!

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:25.950
(The Demon Girl Next Door Season 2)

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:30.950
(The Demon Girl Next Door Season 2)

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:33.330
Shamiko, did you remember?

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:34.870
I can't remember.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:36.960
How about eating something sour?

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:38.290
Sour!

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:41.750
It's a memory from 10 years ago
when she was ill.

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:43.420
It's hard to remember.

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:46.260
Maybe we can use Shamiko's power here.

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:47.970
Shamiko's power?

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:49.800
But this is a secret of the demons,

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:50.140
(I don't want to talk about it)
But this is a secret of the demons,

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:52.770
(I don't want to talk about it)
so I don't want to explain it
in front of Momo and Mikan.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:55.140
What if I give you a Yorishiro ticket?

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:56.730
I'll explain in detail!

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:58.350
What is a Yorishiro ticket?

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:00.560
(What is a Yorishiro ticket?)
It's a ticket that makes your laundry

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:01.610
(What is a Yorishiro ticket?)
whiter than usual!

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:02.900
(What is a Yorishiro ticket?)
That's amazing!

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:03.650
(What is a Yorishiro ticket?)

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:05.190
(What is a Yorishiro ticket?)
That's not true!

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:07.700
(What is a Yorishiro ticket?)
By the way, what is Shamiko's power?

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:09.620
Fine,

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:12.580
I will have to explain it to you.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:12.870
(Yorishiro)

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:16.290
(Yorishiro)
Shamiko's power is the power to dive into dreams.

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:17.540
That was

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.330
(You)
actually a very simplified explanation for you.

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:23.000
You probably wouldn't be able to follow me

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:24.510
even if I explained it to you properly.

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:26.920
That's not true! I'll do my best!

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:27.720
I see.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:29.050
I'll explain it to you.

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:30.050
Please!

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:32.760
The more accurate description of the ability

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:35.060
is to penetrate the emotional
or unemotional unconscious

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:35.430
(Penetrate the emotional or unemotional unconscious)

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:38.640
(Penetrate the emotional or unemotional unconscious)
of any person, animal or inanimate object.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:43.270
Emotional, unemotional,
unconscious, penetrate...

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:43.860
(Strange! emotionless)

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:44.650
(Strange! emotionless)
In other words,

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:46.940
(Strange! emotionless)
there's a creature called "emotionless"

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:48.320
(Strange! emotionless)
and we fight with it.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:50.570
Okay, you're not following me!

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:52.370
The unconscious is

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:56.120
a very deep place in the human mind

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:59.710
where memories
and innate knowledge are stored.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:04.000
We can enter there and peek into it

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:05.750
and tamper with it without permission.

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:07.340
Dreams are like a gateway
to the unconscious realm,

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:08.130
(Zawa)
Dreams are like a gateway to the unconscious realm,

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:09.630
Dreams are like a gateway
to the unconscious realm,

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:10.590
so some people call us dream demons.

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:12.760
(Dream demons)
so some people call us dream demons.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:16.350
In other words, if we
use Shamiko's power on herself,

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:19.730
she may be able to
see her memories from 10 years ago.

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:23.810
Please explain again
from the area of the emotionless.

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:25.900
You're still stuck on that point!?

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:26.730
(Angry)

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:29.950
Can we follow you in your dreams?

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:31.570
No, you can't. You'll get repelled.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:34.200
The reason I can
follow Shamiko into her dream

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.540
is because I am her soulmate.

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:37.910
Momo,

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:40.620
I'll do it on my own.

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:42.420
- Shamiko...
- Are you sure?

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:42.880
(Character 101 Great Gathering!)

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:46.340
(Character 101 Great Gathering!)
Yes, I don't remember much of my childhood,

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:47.170
(Character 101 Great Gathering!)
so I want to see it!

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:49.460
I get it.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:51.260
Dream demons better
get used to it than learn it!

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:54.430
Salvage the information about the core
from your memories and show it!

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:55.510
I'll do my best!

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:57.560
You can watch my bravery here!

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.640
Good night!

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:04.810
Shamiko just looks like a napping girl.

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:09.440
Shamiko!

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:15.320
That's the door to
your memories of ten years ago.

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:17.120
10 years ago?

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.240
It's a hallway all the way down.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.000
It's like a dungeon.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:24.790
Childhood memories are often intricate.

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:28.170
We'll have to search through them
to find the scene where you met the core.

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:31.550
It's hard for a newbie to return from the depths.

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:35.010
So be careful so that I don't lose track of you.

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:35.430
(What should I do in case I get lost?)

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:37.930
(What should I do in case I get lost?)
What should I do in case I get lost?

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:41.230
The more tears you shed,
the stronger you will become.

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:43.560
You will come back with spirit and perseverance!

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:46.060
(Down)
I see. I'll get over it with my spirit.

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:51.240
ancestor, I see something moving!

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:52.190
Is that a core?

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:54.110
No, that's not.

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:56.660
It's your bad memories transformed.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:59.410
Is there such a thing in my heart?

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:01.500
I enjoy a good meal every day.

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:05.000
Everyone has bad memories
if you dig into one's memory.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:07.170
Rather, if you are able to bury them

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:08.540
and smile through them

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:11.210
that means you and
the people around you are healthy.

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:12.010
I see!

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:15.310
I also bury my memories of losing immediately.

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:17.300
Thanks to that, my tail is always wagging!

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:19.300
I see! That's my ancestor!

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:20.510
The worst kind of person

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:23.890
is the one who ruminates over
bad memories over and over again.

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.190
The dreams of such a person

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:27.690
are so muddy and hard to move through.

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:28.980
Muddy...

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:31.780
(Muddy)

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:33.780
(Rumble)

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:38.870
It seems like it would make noise
when it makes contact.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:40.330
Can we do it while hiding?

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.160
Yes! I'll get through it!

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:44.620
Crisis management!

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:06.600
(Mikan) (Sususususu)

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:08.600
(Mikan) (Sususususu)
Sususususu...

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:09.480
Sususususu...

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:13.110
Sususu, susu, sususu.

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.490
Special technique, Demon Stealth!

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:18.240
Can't we hide a little better looking?

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:21.240
Strange, there are so many of them.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:24.160
You've had it tough those days?

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:25.950
They're about to find out
my demonic stealth!

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:27.290
Oh no! Let's run away!

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.500
What happens if I get caught?

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:31.630
It's your memory, so you won't die!

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:34.550
But you'll have nightmares for a few days,

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:35.880
and that's bad for your health!

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:37.920
You should tell me that first!

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:39.800
What should I do?!

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:41.550
Hang in there,
hang in there, hang in there!

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:43.260
Run, run, run!

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:45.270
Okay, I'll figure it out!

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:48.060
Oh no, the noise, I can't hear you.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:48.730
What?

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:50.150
Ancestor?

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.320
Ancestor!

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:57.320
I've lost them.

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:58.780
How shall I explore?

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:00.450
More importantly,
how shall I return home?

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:02.820
Ah, hello.

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:08.410
No ancestors, can't go home, big ghosts!

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:10.080
What shall I do, what shall I do?

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:11.250
You lost her?

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:16.510
The noise brought up a lot of bad memories
that even she had forgotten,

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:17.840
it was unexpected...

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:19.510
What about Shamiko?

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:23.010
She will be lost in the depths
of her own mind for a while

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:25.010
and sleep for a few days.

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:28.060
Does that mean she will be chased
by bad memories throughout that time?

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:30.770
It's a common mistake
for novice dream demons.

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:32.060
No!

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:33.980
You have to wake her up somehow!

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:36.610
That's not a shallow sleep
that can be easily woken up!

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:38.780
It'll only sour her dreams!

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:41.070
I knew I shouldn't have let her do it.

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:43.370
We'll figure out a way to wake her up.

00:19:43.490 --> 00:19:45.530
She'll wake up naturally in a few days.

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:47.450
I want to help her, too!

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:50.370
But think of the trouble
and cost of the search...

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:51.830
Even so!

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:53.580
I'm definitely going to save her!

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:54.670
Momo...

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:59.710
I know I'm not making any sense,

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:02.930
but Shamiko once saved me in a dream.

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:03.800
I have a feeling.

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:06.220
So I don't want
to leave her alone in this situation,

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:10.230
even if it's inefficient
and the evidence is tenuous.

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:12.100
Do something, Lilith!

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:21.900
I don't know what to do! What should I do?

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:24.070
Calm down, calm down.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:27.120
You have a nice weapon, don't you?

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:28.540
Your father's wand.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:30.160
This?

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:32.790
That's right. You know how to use it,

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:34.880
you can transform them into something nice.

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:39.590
Let's turn it into a smart weapon
and get them out.

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:41.010
Okay, I'll do it.

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:44.430
Smart weapon!

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:54.690
Let me explain!

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:57.440
A smart weapon is a weapon

00:20:57.440 --> 00:20:59.900
that can defeat anything only in your dreams!

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:02.940
You can do it!

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:03.490
Thank you,

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.530
(Fluffy)
Thank you,

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:05.780
(Fluffy)

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:07.530
(Fluffy)
you are, uh...

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:07.950
(Fluffy)

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:11.240
You're just a passing memory of meringue,
aren't you!

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:13.370
No, no, no! I'm not a memory!

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:14.750
And it's not a meringue either!

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.000
I've met you twice.

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:17.710
Eh?

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:20.050
I was not able to come to this place.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:21.880
Right now I'm forcing myself to here

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.420
through the medium of your memories.

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:27.430
I want to talk to you as my real look,
so will you help me?

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:29.140
Try to concentrate for a second.

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:30.970
Yeah? Concentrate?

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:33.140
Hold up your wand! Come on!

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:38.310
You can do it! You can do it!
Think you can do it!

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:41.150
Come on!

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:45.570
Good!

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:47.280
The formation is okay.

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:49.200
Thank you for your cooperation!

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:51.160
After 10 years of blanks,

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:03.420
I'm the Sakura bringing good luck to your town!

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:07.880
Here comes the magical girl, Chiyoda Sakura!

00:22:07.880 --> 00:22:09.340
(Silent)

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:11.600
Hey, handshake, handshake!

00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:14.600
Dear sealed father...

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:17.060
Thank you for helping my little sister Momo!

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:19.100
(Whaaaaaaat!)
Whaaaaaaat!

00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:23.480
I was saved by a very important person!

00:23:54.910 --> 00:23:55.910
(Pa)(Next episode)

00:23:55.910 --> 00:23:56.200
(Next episode)

00:23:56.200 --> 00:24:00.290
A very important person saved me
when I was in danger!

00:24:00.290 --> 00:24:02.290
But I lost contact with my ancestor.

00:24:02.290 --> 00:24:03.330
Can I return?

00:24:03.330 --> 00:24:03.790
(Nu)
Can I return?

00:24:03.790 --> 00:24:04.500
(Cha)
Lilith, please tell me how to save Shamiko!

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:06.380
Lilith, please tell me how to save Shamiko!

00:24:06.380 --> 00:24:08.840
(Sunset Oath! The Path of The Demons!)
Wait, wait, Momo, let's calm down and think.

00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:09.880
(Sunset Oath! The Path of The Demons!)
Where's sour food?
